my $CODE = <<'END_CODE';
one
two
three
END_CODE

{
    desc => q{2J joins 2 lines (current + next), reducing 3 lines to 2},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/join_3_lines_2J`

Tests that **2J** joins the current line with the next 2 lines, so
3 lines become 1 joined line. In vim, `NJ` joins N lines (current + N-1 below).

**Keys:** `2J`

**initial.png**
- Buffer has 3 lines: "one", "two", "three"
- Cursor on line 1 at column 0

**after_2J_join.png**
- Buffer has 1 line: "one two three"
- All three lines joined with spaces
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('2J');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_2J_join');
    },
}
